Requirements: 13   with obligations: 10   deliberately none: 3

[task-01] Materializing an archetype fixture into a git repository must commit exactly
    the files the fixture describes, and must produce the same commit identifiers every
    time it runs.
    -> materialize-exact-fixture-files-and-stable-ids  [functional/explicit]
       Materializing an archetype fixture into a git repository commits exactly the
       files described by the fixture and produces the same commit identifiers every
       time it runs.

[constraint-01] The base commit's tree holds exactly the files of the fixture's `base`
    directory, each carrying that file's content.
    -> base-commit-tree-matches-base-directory  [functional/explicit]
       The base commit's tree holds exactly the files of the fixture's `base` directory,
       each carrying that file's content.

[constraint-02] The head commit's tree holds exactly the files of the fixture's `head`
    directory, each carrying that file's content.
    -> head-commit-tree-matches-head-directory  [functional/explicit]
       The head commit's tree holds exactly the files of the fixture's `head` directory,
       each carrying that file's content.

[constraint-03] A file whose content differs between `base` and `head` is committed with
    its head content even when the head file has the same size, mode and modification
    time as the base file it replaced.
    -> head-content-wins-for-same-metadata-change  [functional/explicit]
       A file whose content differs between `base` and `head` is committed with its head
       content even when the head file has the same size, mode and modification time as
       the base file it replaced.

[constraint-04] What a commit records is determined by file content alone, not by the
    modification times of the files on disk.
    -> content-alone-determines-commit-records  [invariant/explicit]
       What a commit records is determined by file content alone, not by the
       modification times of the files on disk.

[constraint-05] What a commit records does not change when git is configured to compare
    a working-tree file against its recorded status using fewer fields.
    -> fewer-working-tree-fields-do-not-change-recorded-content  [compatibility/explicit]
       What a commit records does not change when git is configured to compare a
       working-tree file against its recorded status using fewer fields.

[constraint-06] Materializing one fixture twice produces the same base commit identifier
    both times, and the same head commit identifier both times.
    -> same-commit-ids-on-repeat-materialization  [invariant/explicit]
       Materializing one fixture twice yields the same base commit identifier both times
       and the same head commit identifier both times.

[exclusion-01] Whether a fixture's `base` and `head` trees describe the change they are
    meant to describe.
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       Names whether the fixture trees describe the intended change as out of scope for
       this change.

[exclusion-02] Which archetype fixtures exist, and the ground-truth labels attached to
    them.
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       Names which archetype fixtures exist and their ground-truth labels as out of
       scope for this change.

[exclusion-03] How long materialization takes.
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       Names materialization runtime as out of scope for this change.

[completion-01] A test asserts that a file replaced between base and head by content of
    the same size, mode and modification time is committed with its head content.
    -> test-replaced-file-same-metadata-head-content  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a file replaced between base and head by content of the same
       size, mode and modification time is committed with its head content.

[completion-02] A test asserts that the committed content of every file in a
    materialized fixture equals that file's content in the fixture directory.
    -> test-every-file-committed-content-matches-fixture  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that the committed content of every file in a materialized fixture
       equals that file's content in the fixture directory.

[completion-03] A test asserts that materializing one fixture twice produces the same
    base commit identifier and the same head commit identifier.
    -> test-repeat-materialization-stable-commit-identifiers  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that materializing one fixture twice produces the same base commit
       identifier and the same head commit identifier.

